    "notes": "A Final Lien Ledger is a detailed document summarizing every transaction on the lien: charges, credits, payments and adjustments. Its purpose is to make sure every financial piece is accounted for accurately before we close out the lien with a final payment. Think of it as the reconciliation behind the balance figure."
