    "notes": "Why do providers sell their invoices? This approach is frequently seen in personal injury claims, or any case where immediate payment isn't possible. The third party establishes a lien on the patient's settlement or judgment and essentially waits for payment from the lawsuit's proceeds. For you, that means the company holding the lien may not be the one who treated the client, and it is the one you must verify with."
